+# Hegel Property-Based Testing Report — speedate
+
+## 1. Summary
+
+Added 12 property-based tests (via the `hegeltest` crate, imported as `hegel`) to
+`tests/main.rs` in a new `hegel_properties` module, covering format→parse
+roundtrips for `Date`/`Time`/`DateTime`/`Duration`, parser no-panic robustness,
+rejection of out-of-range calendar/clock components at their exact boundaries,
+timestamp roundtrips, duration sign symmetry, and differential checks against
+chrono. All properties pass at the default case count, at a 10x exploratory run
+(1000 cases each), and the two riskiest properties (duration f64-fraction
+roundtrip and the chrono differential) at 20,000 cases. **No bugs were found**;
+no failing tests are pinned. The full pre-existing suite (482 integration tests,
+49 doc tests) still passes.
+
+Changes: `tests/main.rs` (+~330 lines), `Cargo.toml` (dev-dependency
+`hegeltest`), `.gitignore` (`/.hegel/`).
+
+## 2. Properties Added
+
+Generators (composites): `valid_dates` (year 0–9999, month 1–12, day 1–month
+length with the month-end boundary boosted, leap-year rule transcribed from the
+spec independently of `src/date.rs`), `valid_times` (with optional whole-minute
+tz offsets in ±23:59, the parser's documented domain), `valid_datetimes`,
+`tz_aware_datetimes`, `normalized_durations` (field ranges matching
+`Duration::new`'s normalized output, with year/365-day boundaries boosted).
+
+1. **`prop_date_display_parse_roundtrip`** — any valid calendar date survives
+   `Display` → `parse_str_rfc3339` unchanged; string form is a fixpoint; lax
+   `parse_str` agrees with the strict parser on canonical input.
+2. **`prop_time_display_parse_roundtrip`** — same for `Time`, including
+   microsecond formatting and `Z` / `±HH:MM` offset rendering.
+3. **`prop_datetime_display_parse_roundtrip`** — the crown roundtrip for
+   `DateTime`, plus string fixpoint.
+4. **`prop_parse_never_panics`** — all four parsers (`parse_bytes` and
+   `FromStr`) return `Err` rather than panic on arbitrary Unicode text and on
+   near-miss input (canonical datetime strings with one byte corrupted,
+   including into invalid UTF-8).
+5. **`prop_date_rejects_out_of_range_components`** — month 0, month 13–99,
+   day 0, and day just past the month's length (covers Feb 29 in non-leap
+   years, Feb 30, Apr 31, …) are all rejected by both strict and lax parsers.
+6. **`prop_time_rejects_out_of_range_components`** — hour 24+, minute 60+,
+   second 60+ (leap seconds are documented as unsupported), |tz| ≥ 24h, and
+   tz minutes 60+ are all rejected.
+7. **`prop_datetime_timestamp_roundtrip`** — `DateTime::from_timestamp(ts,
+   micro).timestamp() == ts` across the entire documented seconds range
+   |ts| ≤ 2×10¹⁰, with the watershed and epoch boundaries boosted; microsecond
+   and naïve-tz fields preserved.
+8. **`prop_date_timestamp_roundtrip_second_unit`** — with
+   `TimestampUnit::Second` (no watershed inference), `Date` → `timestamp()` →
+   `from_timestamp` is the identity for every valid date 0000-01-01 to
+   9999-12-31, including dates past the 2×10¹⁰ inference watershed (> year 2603).
+9. **`prop_duration_display_parse_roundtrip`** — normalized `Duration`s survive
+   ISO-8601 `Display` → `parse_str`, exercising the day→year split in Display,
+   fractional-second trimming, and the f64 fraction-parsing path.
+10. **`prop_duration_sign_symmetry`** — `-X` and `+X` parse to the same
+    magnitude with `positive` flipped, and `signed_total_seconds` /
+    `signed_microseconds` / `signed_total_ms` negate exactly.
+11. **`prop_datetime_agrees_with_chrono`** — differential: speedate's canonical
+    tz-aware string parses under `chrono::DateTime::parse_from_rfc3339` and
+    denotes the same instant (`timestamp_tz()` vs chrono's `timestamp()`,
+    matching subsecond micros).
+12. **`prop_datetime_ordering_matches_chrono`** — ordering consistency:
+    `PartialOrd` on two tz-aware `DateTime`s agrees with chrono's
+    instant-based `Ord` on the same values (including equal-instant,
+    different-offset pairs, where both report `Equal`).
+
+## 3. Relationship to Existing Tests and Fuzz Targets
+
+The repo ships five libFuzzer targets (`fuzz/fuzz_targets/`):
+`datetime_from_timestamp` (chrono differential on `(i64, u32)`),
+`datetime_parse_bytes` (chrono differential on inputs chrono also accepts),
+`duration_parse_bytes` (no-panic only), and `parse_int`/`parse_float`
+(std differential). The new properties supplement rather than duplicate them:
+
+- The fuzzers **never test the Display direction**. Formatting was previously
+  covered only by example-based `param_tests!`. The format→parse roundtrips
+  (1, 2, 3, 9) are the main new coverage: they generate *valid structured
+  values* directly, so every case exercises the interesting path, whereas byte
+  fuzzers reach valid dates rarely and valid tz-aware datetimes almost never.
+- `Time` and `Date` had **no fuzz targets at all**; properties 1, 2, 5, 6
+  cover their parsers at exact calendar/clock boundaries.
+- `duration_parse_bytes` checks only "doesn't crash"; properties 9 and 10 add
+  value-level correctness (roundtrip identity and sign algebra), including the
+  f64 fraction arithmetic in `parse_iso_duration`/`parse_number_frac`.
+- Property 8 targets a gap the timestamp fuzzer can't see: the default `Infer`
+  watershed makes `Date::from_timestamp(d.timestamp(), ..)` non-identity for
+  dates past year 2603, so the explicit-`Second`-unit config path is otherwise
+  untested against the full date range.
+- The corrupted-canonical-string branch of property 4 probes the near-miss
+  space (one byte off a valid datetime) far more densely than uniform fuzzing.
+
+Existing unit tests were left untouched; the property tests were added to the
+same file (`tests/main.rs`) per repo convention of a single integration test
+file. No AI-contribution gate (`HUMAN_VS_MACHINE.md`, anti-AI clauses in
+README/LICENSE) was found in the repository.
+
+## 4. Verification (Run and Reflect)
+
+- **Liveness**: temporarily inverted the assertion in
+  `prop_datetime_display_parse_roundtrip`; hegel failed the test and shrank to
+  a near-minimal counterexample (`0000-01-31T00:00:00`), confirming generation
+  and shrinking are live. Reverted, `.hegel/` database removed.
+- **Guarded branch**: the `if let Ok(s) = from_utf8` branch in
+  `prop_parse_never_panics` fires on every text-branch case (~50% of draws),
+  so the `FromStr` checks are not vacuous.
+- **Exploratory high-count run**: all 12 tests run at `test_cases = 1000`
+  (10x default) with a temporary atomic case counter confirming 1000+ cases
+  actually executed (counter printed 200…1200). The two riskiest properties
+  (duration f64-fraction roundtrip, chrono differential) additionally ran at
+  20,000 cases. All passed; counters and case-count attributes then reverted
+  to defaults for the committed tests.
+- **Full suite**: `cargo test` — 494 integration + 49 doc tests pass;
+  `cargo fmt --check` clean; `cargo clippy --tests` introduces no new warnings
+  (remaining `clone_on_copy` warnings are pre-existing in the old test code).
+
+## 5. Findings, Limitations and Recommendations
+
+- **No bugs found.** speedate 0.17.0's parse/format/timestamp core held up
+  under all 12 properties at elevated case counts. This is consistent with the
+  crate being continuously fuzzed; the genuinely new surfaces (Display
+  direction, `Duration` value semantics, explicit timestamp units) were also
+  clean.
+- **Domain caveats encoded in generators (documented in comments):**
+  - Constructed `Time.tz_offset` values are restricted to whole minutes < 24h —
+    that is the parser's own output domain; sub-minute offsets render
+    truncated by `Display` and are unreachable by parsing, so roundtrip is not
+    claimed for them (a `Time { tz_offset: Some(30) }` built by hand displays
+    as `+00:00` — arguably surprising, but no documented contract is violated).
+  - `Duration` roundtrip generates already-normalized field values (what
+    `Duration::new` produces); `Display` is not defined to be injective on
+    denormalized structs.
+  - The `Infer` watershed means numeric-timestamp roundtrips are only asserted
+    on their documented domains (|ts| ≤ 2×10¹⁰ for infer, full range for
+    `TimestampUnit::Second`).
+- **Possible follow-ups**: a differential property against the `iso8601` crate
+  (already a dev-dependency) for `Duration` parsing; porting the
+  `datetime_from_timestamp` fuzzer's chrono model into a hegel property so it
+  runs in CI; property coverage for `in_timezone`/`with_timezone_offset`
+  arithmetic.
